@flexiarg test-registry/fill-forward-not-sweep
@title A Registry Fills Forward; It Does Not Sweep Or Backfill
@keywords registry-service, no-cron, no-backfill, mint-time, observation-time, acceptance-time, starts-empty
@audience registry operators, validation-service designers
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-19 (claude-12; Joe's rulings same day: "I didn't commission a cron sweep. This is a registry service, not a full scan" and "I did not commission a backfill of history either")
@references [test-registry/register-the-run test-registry/bind-the-subject hygiene/settle-with-meters apparatus/monitors-measure-the-work]
@see-also inbox-zero/measure-against-the-remote
@how the ledgers start empty and fill forward at exactly three kinds of moment: a warrant at mint time (an author registered a run), an incident at observation time (someone actually saw warranted behaviour fail), a binding at acceptance time (a reviewer bound a subject to its warrant). No scheduled process walks history or the codebase looking for entries to add. Conformance readout (current/stale/no-warrant) is computed on demand from what the ledger holds, and "the registry has no entry for X" is a legitimate, permanent answer for anything that predates it.
@violation-signature a cron job appending to a registry ledger; entries whose :at is the scan time, not the event time; a launch plan that begins by importing history; ledger growth proportional to elapsed time rather than to events.
! conclusion: Registry entries are appended only when a warrant is minted, an incident is observed, or a binding is accepted; nothing scans and nothing backfills.

  + context: A validation service holds subject bindings and a revalidation queue, and it is tempting to make it "complete".

  + IF:
    Someone proposes a periodic sweep or a historical import to populate the registry.

  + HOWEVER:
    Completeness is the scanner's virtue, not the registry's; the registry's virtue is that every entry was brought by a party with standing, at the time it happened.

  + THEN:
    Decline the sweep and the backfill; let coverage grow exactly as fast as real mints, observations and acceptances arrive.

  + BECAUSE:
    An entry nobody brought is either recomputable on demand (so storing it is a cache posing as evidence) or unattested (so storing it is fabrication).

  + evidence: 2026-09-19 incident: 339 :incident-seen cursor entries written into the durable incidents ledger by review runs (an env-var name error let a scan-style cursor fall through to the durable default) — deleted the same day; the commissioned subjects.ednlog bindings, brought one at a time at acceptance, were kept.
